------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream attributions
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Atlas explicitly extends a small canon of prior work on
exploit-to-defense benchmarks. Each case carries the primary
post-mortem URL in its case README; the upstream benchmarks the
Atlas connects to are:

- Trace2Inv. Chen et al., "Trace2Inv: Demystifying Invariant-Inducing
  Bytecode-Level Vulnerabilities of Smart Contracts," FSE 2024.
  arXiv:2404.14580. 27 historical EVM exploits with paired runtime
  invariant guards. The Atlas's EVM-bridge case set draws from
  Trace2Inv's case set with explicit attribution.

- DeFiHackLabs (SunWeb3Sec). 572 historical EVM exploits reproduced
  as Foundry PoCs. https://github.com/SunWeb3Sec/DeFiHackLabs

- FLAMES. arXiv:2510.21401 (Oct 2025). LLM-synthesized invariants for
  Solidity, defender-side.

- PropertyGPT. LLM-synthesized property-based testing for Solidity.

The Atlas is differentiated against this canon on three axes (cross-VM
into non-EVM; pre-deploy CI gate, not runtime guard; tied to runnable
CaliperForge harnesses) — see README.md "Related work and positioning".

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Affected protocols (post-mortems cited per case)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

- zkLend (Feb 2025): BlockSec, Halborn, zkLend Medium incident report.
- Cetus (May 2025): Dedaub, Halborn, Cyfrin, MerkleScience.
- Cashio (Mar 2022): Helius "Solana Hacks: A Complete History" entry.
- Mango Markets (Oct 2022): Helius entry; post-mortems on the
  Avraham Eisenberg case.
- Loopscale (Apr 2025): protocol-published post-mortem (case README).

The Atlas reconstructs vulnerable code paths from these published
post-mortems for the purpose of demonstrating a defender-side
property test. The reconstructed code is NOT a fork of the protocol
team's production source; it is a same-source twin minimal to the
bug class.

